        <skos:prefLabel xml:lang="de">Waasmunster</skos:prefLabel>
        <skos:definition xml:lang="en">Waasmunster, a municipality in the province of East Flanders, where eight issues of emergency paper money were issued during the First World War, dated 23 October 1914, 28 September 1915, undated (1916, with the municipality name Waesmunster), 25 October 1916, undated (1916?), 1 January 1917 and two undated, one of which bears the municipality name Waesmunster.</skos:definition>
        <dcterms:source rdf:resource="https://wiki.muntenenpapiergeld.nl/index.php?title=Papiergeldplaatsen"/>
